-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt browser playground
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason's [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer,
+compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The home page is prerendered to
+`dist/client/index.html`. Rendering happens entirely in a module Web Worker;
+no rendering API, uploads, cross-origin isolation, or GPU is required.
 
+## Build
 
-```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
-```
+Install Node dependencies with `pnpm install`. Install Emscripten (`em++` must
+be on PATH), then run `pnpm build`. `pnpm build:wasm` rebuilds only the checked-in
+`public/wasm/smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm` artifacts.
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+`native/smallpt.original.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source.
+`native/smallpt.cpp` retains its radiance and sphere-intersection core and replaces
+the file-writing main with progressive RGBA rendering exports. Four subpixel
+samples are accumulated per pass. A 1 MB stack accommodates recursive tracing.
+The browser transfers pixel buffers from the worker to a Canvas 2D context.
+The bundled preview is rendered from the same C++ source, not a substitute for
+the live WebAssembly output.
 
-## Tech Stack
-
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+Randomize changes both sphere colors and the two side-wall colors and restarts
+the render. Palette pickers, quality, resolution, pause/resume, original-scene
+reset, and PNG download are available. The original smallpt code is MIT licensed;
+see `native/LICENSE.txt`.
